From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] variables.yaml: every variable names the stages that read it

41 variables had no `stages:` list. The list is what a build system uses
to know which stages a variable reaches; a variable without one can only
be treated as reaching every stage, and then setting ENABLE_DPO, a
detail-placement knob, re-runs synthesis, floorplan and everything else
of every block of a hierarchical design -- measured on a 34-block
XiangShan: the change of a placement polish cost a full pass of block
synthesis.

The scopes come from where flow/scripts reads each variable: ENABLE_DPO
and DPO_MAX_DISPLACEMENT in detail_place.tcl (place); CAP_MARGIN and
SLEW_MARGIN through repair_design_helper from resize.tcl and
global_route.tcl; RECOVER_POWER and GENERATE_ARTIFACTS_ON_FAILURE in
global_route.tcl; TAP_CELL_NAME, FASTROUTE_TCL and MIN_CLK_ROUTING_LAYER
in the floorplan; USE_FILL, FILL_CONFIG and REPAIR_PDN_VIA_LAYER in
detailed route; the klayout and RCX inputs in final; AUTO_MEMORIES in
synth. The design, platform and library identifiers every stage loads
say `All stages` explicitly, as the flow's own use of that value already
allows. docs/user/FlowVariables.md and variables.json are regenerated
with generate-variables-docs.py and yaml_to_json.py.

Not upstreamed; carried by bazel-orfs. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS
whose variables.yaml has a stages list for every variable.
---
